 "answer_to_user": "The nuclear-fuel supply chain splits into two buckets. MINERS (Uranium Mining & Development): Cameco (CCJ.US) is the anchor, alongside NexGen Energy (NXE.US), Energy Fuels (UUUU.US), Denison Mines (DNN.US), plus China's CGN Mining (1164.HK) and CNNC International (2302.HK); Japanese trading houses Mitsui (8031.JP) and Marubeni (8002.JP) show up as secondary exposure. ENRICHMENT / CONVERSION (HALEU): Centrus Energy (LEU.US) is the pure-play US enricher, with Cameco again, X-Energy (XE.US), Standard Nuclear (STDN.US), ASP Isotopes (ASPI.US), and BWX Technologies (BWXT.US), Oklo (OKLO.US) and Nano Nuclear (NNE.US) as secondary. So a 'nuclear revival' basket = Cameco + NexGen + Energy Fuels + Denison on the mining side and Centrus + ASP Isotopes + X-Energy on the enrichment side, trading across the US, Hong Kong and Japan."
